Parts carried over from that project:
  - Bluetooth (BLE) input and connection tuning: device discovery, parameter
    negotiation, 7.5 ms policy, rate diagnostics, battery / charge decoding
  - Haptics and motion: DualSense HID haptic feedback, HD rumble passthrough,
    rumble queue and pacing, IMU motion pipeline

Modifications (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b)):
Every file carrying the code above has been modified, not copied verbatim. The
namespace was changed from Y700Switch2V60Viiper to Pro2Plus in all of them, and
they were rewritten in place while keeping the upstream structure and protocol
handling. Everything else in this repository is this project's own code.

Third-party components keep their own licenses:
  - Viiper (GPL-3.0)      https://github.com/Alia5/VIIPER
  - usbip-win2 (BSD-2-Clause)  https://github.com/vadimgrn/usbip-win2
  - libusb (LGPL-2.1)     https://github.com/libusb/libusb

libusb is bundled unmodified as a standalone DLL and called via P/Invoke; it can
be replaced with any compatible build. Its source is available at the repository
above.

Viiper is shipped as a separate executable and run as a child process over a
local port; it is not linked or combined with this project's source, so it is
mere aggregation and does not change the licensing of this project.

The shipped viiper-haptic-v2.8.exe is a modified build derived from VIIPER by
the upstream project (SHA-256 F434E356...7FEBFC). Per GPL-3.0 section 6, its
corresponding source is the upstream repository's
source/final-three-in-one/tools/viiper/haptic-src at tag pro2-v3.2.7, not the
pristine VIIPER release.

